my definition of success  so i got a tweet that came in love you  guys from anthony who wrote in to say  evan how do you define success  for me success is a pretty simple  pretty simple answer it's being happy i  think people who are happy  are successful maybe that's different  than what most people will look at most  people look at  you know how much money you're making  what companies you started  or you know what what job title you have  for me that doesn't it doesn't matter  because you could be the richest person  in the world you could be the most  most successful person i guess in the  world in terms of how much money you  have but if you're not happy if you're  not enjoying what you have  well then in my mind at least you're not  successful the concept of happiness  is is a hard one and we all know what it  feels like to be happy  and some people are way happier than  others nobody's happy all the time  though  nobody is happy all the time you know  those people put on that  or have always been happy they're faking  it some of the time  and you have to understand what is it  that makes you happy i think for  for different people it's different  things so all i can share is what makes  me happy  the three things that make me happy are  freedom growth  and impact so freedom i need to feel  like i'm in control of my own time  when i'm not in control of what i do i  get very frustrated and  upset so that's why it's hard for me to  work for somebody else to have a job  it's hard for me to do things that i  don't like doing  because it makes money i don't i don't  enjoy that stuff i need the freedom  if i want to go off and take half a day  off to go to starbucks and enjoy the  weather outside and have a frappuccino i  can do that if i want to fly to paris  for the weekend just because i can do  that i have the freedom to do that i  need freedom  to be happy growth  i need to feel like i'm i'm learning  constantly  if i'm not learning something new in  some area 